{"bendscript":"0.1","blocks":[{"id":"blk-84751","kind":"heading","level":1,"spans":[{"id":"spn-117474","text":"SpecPrompt — Implementation Build Prompt"}]},{"id":"blk-84752","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-117475","marks":["bold"],"text":"Version:"},{"id":"spn-117476","text":" 1.0 | "},{"id":"spn-117477","marks":["bold"],"text":"Date:"},{"id":"spn-117478","text":" April 2026 | "},{"id":"spn-117479","marks":["bold"],"text":"Type:"},{"id":"spn-117480","text":" Full Implementation (CLI + MCP + Supabase)"}]},{"id":"blk-84753","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-117481","text":"Your Mission"}]},{"id":"blk-84754","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-117482","text":"You are building "},{"id":"spn-117483","marks":["bold"],"text":"SpecPrompt"},{"id":"spn-117484","text":" — the standards layer of the [&] Protocol dark factory pipeline. SpecPrompt defines the SPEC.md format (machine-parseable agent specifications) and provides the CLI toolchain, MCP server, and Supabase registry that make specs the entry point for autonomous code generation."}]},{"id":"blk-84755","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-117485","marks":["bold"],"text":"Read `docs/spec/README.md` fully before writing a single line."},{"id":"spn-117486","text":" It is the authoritative spec."}]},{"id":"blk-84756","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-117487","text":"SpecPrompt is the "},{"id":"spn-117488","marks":["bold"],"text":"first stage"},{"id":"spn-117489","text":" of the dark factory pipeline:"}]},{"id":"blk-84757","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"SpecPrompt (spec in) → Agentelic (build) → OS-008 (enforce) → FleetPrompt (distribute) → RuneFort (observe)"},{"id":"blk-84758","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-117490","text":"Target Stack"}]},{"id":"blk-84759","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"Language:   Elixir 1.17+ / OTP 27\nCLI:        Mix escript (specprompt validate, lint, test-gen, test-compile, diff, publish)\nMCP:        JSON-RPC over HTTP (spec_validate, spec_lint, spec_generate, spec_test_gen,\n            spec_test_compile, spec_test_approve, spec_diff, spec_search)\nDatabase:   PostgreSQL via shared Supabase (spec.* schema, migration range TBD)\nAuth:       Supabase Auth (shared [&] ecosystem — amp.profiles, amp.workspaces)\nParser:     PEG grammar (see spec section 4.4) — implement in both Elixir and TypeScript\nTesting:    ExUnit (Elixir), Vitest (TypeScript parser)\nDeploy:     Fly.io (MCP server) + npm (TypeScript parser)"},{"id":"blk-84760","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-117491","text":"Dual-Mode Architecture"}]},{"id":"blk-84761","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-117492","text":"SpecPrompt operates in two modes. Both must work from day one:"}]},{"id":"blk-84762","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-117493","text":"Filesystem Mode (default, zero-cost)"}]},{"id":"blk-84763","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-84765","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-117494","text":"CLI reads "},{"id":"spn-117495","marks":["code"],"text":".md"},{"id":"spn-117496","text":" files from local git repos"}]}],"id":"blk-84764","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-84767","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-117497","text":"No auth, no database, no network"}]}],"id":"blk-84766","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-84769","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-117498","text":"All tools work offline: validate, lint, test-gen, test-compile, diff"}]}],"id":"blk-84768","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-84771","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-117499","text":"Audit via git history"}]}],"id":"blk-84770","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-84773","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-117500","text":"This is the \"PULSE scales down\" demonstration"}]}],"id":"blk-84772","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-84774","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-117501","text":"Registry Mode (multi-tenant dark factory)"}]},{"id":"blk-84775","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-84777","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-117502","text":"Specs stored in Supabase "},{"id":"spn-117503","marks":["code"],"text":"spec.specs"},{"id":"spn-117504","text":" table"}]}],"id":"blk-84776","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-84779","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-117505","text":"Workspace-scoped via "},{"id":"spn-117506","marks":["code"],"text":"amp.workspaces"}]}],"id":"blk-84778","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-84781","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-117507","text":"Auth via Supabase Auth (same identity as all [&] products)"}]}],"id":"blk-84780","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-84783","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-117508","text":"Visibility: private | workspace | public"}]}],"id":"blk-84782","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-84785","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-117509","text":"Pipeline triggers via Supabase Realtime or CloudEvents webhooks"}]}],"id":"blk-84784","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-84787","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-117510","text":"Required for dark factory automation"}]}],"id":"blk-84786","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-84788","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-117511","text":"Repository Structure"}]},{"id":"blk-84789","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-117512","text":"Create this structure inside "},{"id":"spn-117513","marks":["code"],"text":"specprompt.com/"},{"id":"spn-117514","text":":"}]},{"id":"blk-84790","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"specprompt.com/\n├── lib/\n│   ├── specprompt/\n│   │   ├── parser.ex              # PEG-based SPEC.md parser (section 4.3-4.4)\n│   │   ├── spec.ex                # SpecPrompt.Spec Ecto schema (section 4.6)\n│   │   ├── capability.ex          # SpecPrompt.Capability embedded schema\n│   │   ├── constraint.ex          # SpecPrompt.Constraint embedded schema\n│   │   ├── acceptance_test.ex     # SpecPrompt.AcceptanceTest embedded schema\n│   │   ├── compiled_test.ex       # SpecPrompt.CompiledTest embedded schema (NEW)\n│   │   ├── dependency.ex          # SpecPrompt.Dependency embedded schema\n│   │   ├── changelog_entry.ex     # SpecPrompt.ChangelogEntry embedded schema\n│   │   ├── validator.ex           # Validation rules (section 4.7 — all MUST + SHOULD rules)\n│   │   ├── linter.ex              # Best-practice linting\n│   │   ├── differ.ex              # Spec version diffing\n│   │   ├── test_generator.ex      # Generate test scaffolding from acceptance tests\n│   │   ├── test_compiler.ex       # Compile natural language tests → Agentelic DSL assertions (NEW)\n│   │   ├── publisher.ex           # Publish to FleetPrompt registry or Supabase\n│   │   ├── registry.ex            # Supabase registry client (spec.specs CRUD)\n│   │   ├── interop/\n│   │   │   ├── ampersand.ex       # Bidirectional ampersand.json mapping (section 4.8)\n│   │   │   └── adl.ex             # Bidirectional ADL mapping (section 4.8)\n│   │   └── mcp/\n│   │       ├── server.ex          # MCP JSON-RPC server (section 4.2)\n│   │       └── tools.ex           # Tool definitions and handlers\n│   ├── specprompt.ex              # Application entry point\n│   └── cli.ex                     # CLI escript entry point\n├── test/\n│   ├── parser_test.exs\n│   ├── validator_test.exs\n│   ├── linter_test.exs\n│   ├── test_compiler_test.exs\n│   ├── differ_test.exs\n│   └── fixtures/\n│       ├── valid_spec.md          # Use the customer-support example from spec section 3.3\n│       ├── invalid_spec.md        # Missing required sections\n│       └── compiled_tests.json    # Pre-compiled test assertions\n├── npm/                           # TypeScript parser package (@specprompt/parser)\n│   ├── src/\n│   │   ├── parser.ts\n│   │   ├── types.ts\n│   │   └── index.ts\n│   ├── test/\n│   │   └── parser.test.ts\n│   ├── package.json\n│   └── tsconfig.json\n├── mix.exs\n├── Dockerfile\n└── fly.toml"},{"id":"blk-84791","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-117515","text":"Implementation Order"}]},{"id":"blk-84792","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-117516","text":"Phase 1: Parser + Validator (week 1)"}]},{"id":"blk-84793","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-84795","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-117517","marks":["bold"],"text":"Implement PEG parser"},{"id":"spn-117518","text":" ("},{"id":"spn-117519","marks":["code"],"text":"lib/specprompt/parser.ex"},{"id":"spn-117520","text":")"}]}],"id":"blk-84794","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true},{"id":"blk-84796","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-84798","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-117521","text":"Parse YAML frontmatter (all fields from spec section 4.5, including new "},{"id":"spn-117522","marks":["code"],"text":"workspace_id"},{"id":"spn-117523","text":", "},{"id":"spn-117524","marks":["code"],"text":"visibility"},{"id":"spn-117525","text":", "},{"id":"spn-117526","marks":["code"],"text":"source_hash"},{"id":"spn-117527","text":")"}]}],"id":"blk-84797","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-84800","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-117528","text":"Parse H2 sections: Purpose, Capabilities, Constraints, Acceptance Tests, Architecture, Dependencies, Changelog"}]}],"id":"blk-84799","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-84802","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-117529","text":"Extract structured data into "},{"id":"spn-117530","marks":["code"],"text":"SpecPrompt.Spec"},{"id":"spn-117531","text":" schema"}]}],"id":"blk-84801","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-84804","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-117532","text":"Compute "},{"id":"spn-117533","marks":["code"],"text":"source_hash"},{"id":"spn-117534","text":" (SHA-256 of raw SPEC.md content)"}]}],"id":"blk-84803","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-84806","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-117535","text":"Return "},{"id":"spn-117536","marks":["code"],"text":"{:ok, %SpecPrompt.Spec{}}"},{"id":"spn-117537","text":" or "},{"id":"spn-117538","marks":["code"],"text":"{:error, [errors]}"}]}],"id":"blk-84805","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-84807","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-84809","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-117539","marks":["bold"],"text":"Implement validator"},{"id":"spn-117540","text":" ("},{"id":"spn-117541","marks":["code"],"text":"lib/specprompt/validator.ex"},{"id":"spn-117542","text":")"}]}],"id":"blk-84808","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true,"start":2},{"id":"blk-84810","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-84812","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-117543","text":"All 8 MUST rules from spec section 4.7"}]}],"id":"blk-84811","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-84814","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-117544","text":"All 7 SHOULD warnings (including 3 new compiled test warnings)"}]}],"id":"blk-84813","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-84816","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-117545","text":"Return structured validation result with line numbers"}]}],"id":"blk-84815","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-84817","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-84819","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-117546","marks":["bold"],"text":"Implement CLI"},{"id":"spn-117547","text":" ("},{"id":"spn-117548","marks":["code"],"text":"lib/cli.ex"},{"id":"spn-117549","text":")"}]}],"id":"blk-84818","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true,"start":3},{"id":"blk-84820","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-84822","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-117550","marks":["code"],"text":"specprompt validate SPEC.md"},{"id":"spn-117551","text":" — parse + validate, exit 0/1"}]}],"id":"blk-84821","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-84824","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-117552","marks":["code"],"text":"specprompt lint SPEC.md"},{"id":"spn-117553","text":" — validate + SHOULD warnings"}]}],"id":"blk-84823","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-84825","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-84827","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-117554","marks":["bold"],"text":"Write tests"},{"id":"spn-117555","text":" against the customer-support example from spec section 3.3"}]}],"id":"blk-84826","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true,"start":4},{"id":"blk-84828","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-117556","text":"Phase 2: Test Compilation (week 2)"}]},{"id":"blk-84829","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-117557","text":"This is the critical dark factory bridge — turning natural language acceptance tests into executable assertions."}]},{"id":"blk-84830","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-84832","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-117558","marks":["bold"],"text":"Implement test compiler"},{"id":"spn-117559","text":" ("},{"id":"spn-117560","marks":["code"],"text":"lib/specprompt/test_compiler.ex"},{"id":"spn-117561","text":")"}]}],"id":"blk-84831","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true},{"id":"blk-84833","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-84835","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-117562","text":"Input: "},{"id":"spn-117563","marks":["code"],"text":"%SpecPrompt.Spec{}"},{"id":"spn-117564","text":" with "},{"id":"spn-117565","marks":["code"],"text":"acceptance_tests"}]}],"id":"blk-84834","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-84837","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-117566","text":"For each acceptance test, generate a "},{"id":"spn-117567","marks":["code"],"text":"%SpecPrompt.CompiledTest{}"},{"id":"spn-117568","text":":"}]}],"id":"blk-84836","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-84839","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-117569","marks":["code"],"text":"setup"},{"id":"spn-117570","text":": mocked tool states derived from the "},{"id":"spn-117571","marks":["code"],"text":"given"},{"id":"spn-117572","text":" clause"}]}],"id":"blk-84838","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-84841","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-117573","marks":["code"],"text":"input"},{"id":"spn-117574","text":": agent input derived from the "},{"id":"spn-117575","marks":["code"],"text":"given"},{"id":"spn-117576","text":" clause"}]}],"id":"blk-84840","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-84843","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-117577","marks":["code"],"text":"assertions"},{"id":"spn-117578","text":": list of Agentelic DSL assertions:"}]}],"id":"blk-84842","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-84845","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-117579","marks":["code"],"text":"%{type: :contains, value: \"...\"}"},{"id":"spn-117580","text":" — expected text in output"}]}],"id":"blk-84844","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-84847","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-117581","marks":["code"],"text":"%{type: :tool_called, tool: \"...\", args: %{}}"},{"id":"spn-117582","text":" — expected tool invocation"}]}],"id":"blk-84846","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-84849","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-117583","marks":["code"],"text":"%{type: :tool_not_called, tool: \"...\"}"},{"id":"spn-117584","text":" — forbidden tool invocation"}]}],"id":"blk-84848","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-84851","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-117585","marks":["code"],"text":"%{type: :escalated, value: true/false}"},{"id":"spn-117586","text":" — escalation check"}]}],"id":"blk-84850","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-84853","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-117587","marks":["code"],"text":"%{type: :constraint_respected, constraint_index: N}"},{"id":"spn-117588","text":" — constraint enforcement"}]}],"id":"blk-84852","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-84855","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-117589","text":"Compilation is "},{"id":"spn-117590","marks":["bold"],"text":"LLM-assisted on first pass"},{"id":"spn-117591","text":": send the spec + acceptance test to an LLM, ask it to generate the assertion mapping"}]}],"id":"blk-84854","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-84857","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-117592","text":"Cache compiled tests by "},{"id":"spn-117593","marks":["code"],"text":"{source_hash, test_index}"},{"id":"spn-117594","text":" — unchanged tests reuse prior compilations"}]}],"id":"blk-84856","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-84859","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-117595","text":"Mark all compiled tests as "},{"id":"spn-117596","marks":["code"],"text":"approved: false"},{"id":"spn-117597","text":" initially"}]}],"id":"blk-84858","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-84860","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-84862","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-117598","marks":["bold"],"text":"Implement approval workflow"}]}],"id":"blk-84861","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true,"start":2},{"id":"blk-84863","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-84865","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-117599","marks":["code"],"text":"specprompt test-compile SPEC.md --output tests/compiled.json"},{"id":"spn-117600","text":" — compile all tests"}]}],"id":"blk-84864","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-84867","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-117601","marks":["code"],"text":"specprompt test-compile SPEC.md --approve"},{"id":"spn-117602","text":" — mark all compiled tests as approved"}]}],"id":"blk-84866","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-84869","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-117603","marks":["code"],"text":"specprompt test-compile SPEC.md --status"},{"id":"spn-117604","text":" — show compilation + approval status"}]}],"id":"blk-84868","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-84871","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-117605","text":"Only approved tests are used by Agentelic in the dark factory pipeline"}]}],"id":"blk-84870","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-84872","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-84874","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-117606","marks":["bold"],"text":"Important constraint"},{"id":"spn-117607","text":": The test compiler itself does NOT call LLMs. It generates a structured prompt that an external LLM (via Agente